  "title": "Risk-Aware Occupancy for Safety-Oriented End-to-End Autonomous Driving",
  "summary": "This study proposes a dense, risk-aware occupancy representation for end-to-end autonomous driving systems, improving safety by encoding spatial and temporal risk evidence into a unified BEV map. It introduces a risk-aware occupancy framework (RiskOcc4D-nuScenes) that enhances safety planning with relative open-loop collision reductions of 52.9% and 35.0% under specific metrics.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The paper introduces a RiskOcc4D-nuScenes framework for risk-aware occupancy with 52.9% relative open-loop collision reductions.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The paper demonstrates an improvement of 7.7% in selected-trajectory PDMS and 30.2% in candidate PDMS in challenging scenes.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The RiskOcc4D-nuScenes model uses a dense representation and temporally aligned query structure for improved safety.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
